        <h2>A Word from Brother Aaron</h2>

        <p>
            I am a shepherd, not a gatekeeper. My goal is not to police this community but to
            protect it&mdash;so that the people who most need a safe space to ask their honest
            questions can find one here.
        </p>
        <p>
            These guidelines exist because I take seriously the responsibility of opening this
            door. Everyone who walks through it deserves to be treated with dignity. That includes
            the lifelong saint, the recent convert, the skeptic, the wounded, the questioning,
            and the person who is not sure why they came but felt something pull them here.
            The theological foundation of this community is not decoration. It is the reason
            these rules exist and the authority by which they are enforced.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you ever have a question about these guidelines, or want to raise something you
            are not sure how to categorize, my contact form is always open.
